Ludwerk: SDL's GPU integration with OpenXR, backported onto 3.4.18.

SDL's development line gained an OpenXR integration on its GPU API
(libsdl-org/SDL pull request 14837, merged 2026-01-30, for 3.6.0, which is
not released): the GPU device made on the adapter an OpenXR runtime asks for,
with the instance and device extensions OpenXR needs, a session
(SDL_CreateGPUXRSession) and swapchains whose images are SDL_GPUTextures
(SDL_CreateGPUXRSwapchain), on D3D12, Vulkan and Metal, with the OpenXR
loader loaded at run time. This is that pull request applied to the pinned
release: 26 of its files apply as they are, and the hunks that did not are
list entries (the dynamic API's three lists, the build's option, the
Visual Studio project) and one field of a Vulkan struct, added by hand. The
Khronos headers it carries come as they are (Apache-2.0 OR MIT).

Drop it when a pinned SDL release carries the integration (ADR 0244).

